UN R150.how_it_applies:
UN R150 applies only to the retro-reflector part of this rear lamp (P-05). It is a red rear retro-reflector built into a combined rear lamp of an M1 vehicle, and R48 requires one at the rear. The retro-reflector needs its own R150 approval as a Class IA or IB retro-reflector for motor vehicles. Under 'Classes and variants' the card defines Class IA as an independent retro-reflector and Class IB as a retro-reflector combined with signal lamps that are not watertight. The class therefore depends on whether the lamp housing counts as watertight. Its approval mark can be grouped with the lamp's other marks. The rear position, stop and reversing lamps, the LED modules and the electronics are outside R150; they fall under R148, R10 and R48. The retro-reflector must meet:
- the shape and dimension rules for Class IA/IB;
- the photometric limits (coefficient of luminous intensity, CIL) and the colorimetric limits for red;
- the resistance tests: heat, water penetration (or the moisture and dust alternative for IB), corrosion, rear face if mirror-backed, fuels and lubricating oils;
- the marking and conformity-of-production provisions.
